That's the simplest possible formula.&nbsp;
And then for each subsequent formula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:29.680 --> 02:23:36.320
I'm going to say take the number that's right&nbsp;
above and to that add the number that's to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:36.319 --> 02:23:44.240
the left. Okay, so one above and add one to&nbsp;
the left. And if I take that and drag it down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:45.359 --> 02:23:50.399
you'll see that in each point, it's taking the&nbsp;
number that's immediately above and the number&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:50.399 --> 02:23:55.359
that's immediately to the left and adding them&nbsp;
up, and I get a running total of by the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:55.359 --> 02:24:00.479
I get to the bottom here 110. That actually is&nbsp;
a useful thing to do. If you're keeping track,&nbsp;&nbsp;

